// (inv)-[:CONTAINS_SET]->(nestedSet)-[:HAS_INVENTORY]->(nestedInv)
// OR
// (inv)-[:CONTAINS_MINIFIG]->(minifig)-[:HAS_INVENTORY]->(minifigInv)

// And the final step is:
// (inv)-[:HAS_PART]->(part)

// So a path of depth 0 is: (rootInv)-[:HAS_PART]->(part)
// A path of depth 1 is: (rootInv)-[:CONTAINS_SET]->(s1)-[:HAS_INVENTORY]->(inv1)-[:HAS_PART]->(part)
//                      OR (rootInv)-[:CONTAINS_MINIFIG]->(m1)-[:HAS_INVENTORY]->(inv1)-[:HAS_PART]->(part)

// We can use a variable-length pattern that matches sequences of these "expansion" steps followed by a HAS_PART.
